Kvass","dish/kvass"]]],["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine",[["Kvass","dish/kvass"]]],["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine",[["Gochujang","dish/gochujang"]]],["Latvian cuisine","cuisine/latvian-cuisine",[["Kvass","dish/kvass"]]],["Lithuanian cuisine","cuisine/lithuanian-cuisine",[["Kvass","dish/kvass"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Kvass","dish/kvass"]]],["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Coconut candy","dish/coconut-candy"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Coconut cream","ingredient/coconut-cream"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Chili powder","ingredient/chili-powder"],["Glutinous rice","ingredient/glutinous-rice"],["Gochu-garu","ingredient/gochu-garu"],["Meju","ingredient/meju"],["Rye bread","ingredient/rye-bread"],["Rye flour","ingredient/rye-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/98/Gr%C3%BCnmalz.jpg/500px-Gr%C3%BCnmalz.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Peter Schill","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0 de","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/de/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gr%C3%BCnmalz.jpg"}},"ingredient/louis-dressing":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/louis-dressing","n":"Louis dressing","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Louis dressing is a salad dressing based on mayonnaise, to which red chili sauce, minced green onions, and minced green chili peppers have been added.  It is commonly used as a dressing for salads featuring seafood, such as a crab (Crab Louis) or shrimp (Shrimp Louis)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-louis-dressing"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_dressing"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states",[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Asparagus","ingredient/asparagus"],["Crab meat","ingredient/crab-meat"],["Hard-boiled egg","ingredient/hard-boiled-egg"],["Iceberg lettuce","ingredient/iceberg-lettuce"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6c/Crab_Louie_Salad.jpg/500px-Crab_Louie_Salad.jpg","w":500,"h":396,"by":"Waspstar","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crab_Louie_Salad.jpg"}},"ingredient/raw-milk":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/raw-milk","n":"Raw milk","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Raw milk or unpasteurized milk is milk that has not undergone pasteurization, a process of heating foods to kill pathogens for safe consumption and extension of shelf life."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-raw-milk"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raw_milk"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",[["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ewe's milk","ingredient/ewe-s-milk"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Rennet","ingredient/rennet"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/bb/Bouteilles_commerce_lait_cru_vache_Aveyron_sud.JPG/500px-Bouteilles_commerce_lait_cru_vache_Aveyron_sud.JPG","w":500,"h":536,"by":"Lesyeuxpourvoir","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bouteilles_commerce_lait_cru_vache_Aveyron_sud.JPG"}},"dish/dutch-baby-pancake":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dutch-baby-pancake","n":"Dutch baby pancake","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Western American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A Dutch baby pancake, sometimes called a German pancake, a Bismarck, a Dutch puff, hooligan, or a hootenanny, is a dish that is similar to a large Yorkshire pudding."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dutch-baby-pancake"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_baby_pancake"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"More from Western American cuisine","links":[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"],["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d8/Dutch_Babies.jpg/500px-Dutch_Babies.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Scott Swigart","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dutch_Babies.jpg"}},"dish/eggplant-jam":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/eggplant-jam","n":"Eggplant jam","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Eggplant jam is a whole-fruit jam in  Azerbaijani, Turkish and Syrian cuisine. In Turkey, it is especially popular in Antalya, Iğdır and Kağızman. The Governorate of Iğdır Province is making efforts to obtain a geographical indication for the name \"patlıcan reçeli\". In Syria, it is prepared in a similar way but sometimes topped with coconut flakes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-eggplant-jam"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant_jam"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Azerbaijani cuisine","cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine"],["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine"],["Syrian cuisine","cuisine/syrian-cuisine"],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Syrup","ingredient/syrup"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Georgian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"georgianrecipes.net","note":"Recipe site dedicated to traditional Georgian dishes.","url":"https://georgianrecipes.net/about-georgian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Azerbaijani cuisine","links":[["Badambura","dish/badambura"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Doghramaj","dish/doghramaj"],["Dovga","dish/dovga"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Shekerbura","dish/shekerbura"],["Sheki halva","dish/sheki-halva"],["Shorgoghal","dish/shorgoghal"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b8/Eggplant_jam_Azerbaijan.jpg/500px-Eggplant_jam_Azerbaijan.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Irada","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eggplant_jam_Azerbaijan.jpg"}},"dish/jibneh-arabieh":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/jibneh-arabieh","n":"Jibneh Arabieh","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Jibneh Arabieh is a soft white cheese found all over the Middle East. It is particularly popular in the Persian Gulf region. The cheese has a mild taste similar to feta but less salty. The heritage of the product started with Bedouins using goat or sheep milk; however, current practice is to use cow's milk to make the cheese. Jibneh Arabieh is used for cooking, or simply as a table cheese."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-jibneh-arabieh"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jibneh_Arabieh"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Lebanese cuisine","cuisine/lebanese-cuisine"],["Levantine cuisine","cuisine/levantine-cuisine"],["Palestinian cuisine","cuisine/palestinian-cuisine"],["Syrian cuisine","cuisine/syrian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Goat milk","ingredient/goat-milk"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sheep milk","ingredient/sheep-milk"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Maureen Abood","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"maureenabood.com","note":"Lebanese-American writer Maureen Abood's blog of classic and modern Lebanese recipes.","url":"https://maureenabood.com/blog/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Lebanese cuisine","links":[["Makanek","dish/makanek"],["Meghli","dish/meghli"],["Qatayef","dish/qatayef"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8a/%D8%AC%D8%A8%D9%861.jpg/500px-%D8%AC%D8%A8%D9%861.jpg","w":500,"h":376,"by":"Rotana Nawwaf Al Hasanat","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%AC%D8%A8%D9%861.jpg"}},"ingredient/rempeyek":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/rempeyek","n":"Rempeyek","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Rempeyek or peyek is a deep-fried savoury Indonesian-Javanese cracker made from flour (usually rice flour) with other ingredients, bound or coated by crispy flour batter. The most common type of rempeyek is peyek kacang (\"peanut peyek\"); However, other ingredients can be used instead, such as teri (dried anchovies), rebon (small shrimp), or ebi (dried shrimp). Today, rempeyek is commonly found in Indonesia and Malaysia, as well as in countries with considerable Indonesian migrant populations, such as The Netherlands and Suriname."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rempeyek"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rempeyek"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Javanese cuisine","cuisine/javanese-cuisine",[["Nasi ambeng","dish/nasi-ambeng"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Perkedel","ingredient/perkedel"],["Rendang","ingredient/rendang"],["Sambal","ingredient/sambal"],["Tempeh","ingredient/tempeh"],["Urap","ingredient/urap"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2c/Rempeyek_kacang_tanah.JPG/500px-Rempeyek_kacang_tanah.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Midori","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rempeyek_kacang_tanah.JPG"}},"dish/qeema-najafi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/qeema-najafi","n":"Qeema Najafi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Iraqi cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Qeema Najafi is a traditional Najafi Iraqi dish that is widely popular in Iraq, including in cities such as Baghdad, Karbala, Najaf, and many other Iraqi cities. It was first prepared by the people of Najaf in Iraq. It differs in its method of preparation from Qeema, one of the most famous stews in Iraq and Iran."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-qeema-najafi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qeema_Najafi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Iraqi cuisine","cuisine/iraqi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Chickpea","ingredient/chickpea"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tomato paste","ingredient/tomato-paste"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Iraqi Family Cookbook","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"iraqifamilycookbook.blogspot.com","note":"Long-running blog of Iraqi family recipes tied to the cookbook of the same name.","url":"https://iraqifamilycookbook.blogspot.com/2014","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Iraqi cuisine","links":[["Khubz al-ʾAbbas","dish/khubz-al-abbas"]]}]},"dish/shark-fin-soup":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/shark-fin-soup","n":"Shark fin soup","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Shark fin soup is a soup or stewed dish served in parts of China, Taiwan, and Southeast Asia. The shark fins provide texture, while the taste comes from the other ingredients. As one of the four sea delicacies, it is commonly served at special occasions such as weddings and banquets, or as a luxury item."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-shark-fin-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_fin_soup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Shark meat","ingredient/shark-meat"],["Shark's fin","ingredient/shark-s-fin"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Fuqi feipian","dish/fuqi-feipian"],["Gaifan","dish/gaifan"],["Goubuli","dish/goubuli"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Huangqiao sesame cake","dish/huangqiao-sesame-cake"],["Imitation shark fin soup","dish/imitation-shark-fin-soup"],["Jiaozi","dish/jiaozi"],["Jiuqu","dish/jiuqu"],["Kung Pao chicken","dish/kung-pao-chicken"],["Lanzhou beef noodles","dish/lanzhou-beef-noodles"],["Liangfen","dish/liangfen"],["Lo mai chi","dish/lo-mai-chi"],["Mao xue wang","dish/mao-xue-wang"],["Mapo tofu","dish/mapo-tofu"],["Mianwo","dish/mianwo"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Orange cuttlefish","dish/orange-cuttlefish"],["Osmanthus cake","dish/osmanthus-cake"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/39/Chinese_cuisine-Shark_fin_soup-01.jpg/500px-Chinese_cuisine-Shark_fin_soup-01.jpg","w":500,"h":752,"by":"chee.hong","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinese_cuisine-Shark_fin_soup-01.jpg"}},"ingredient/nam-phrik-phao":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/nam-phrik-phao","n":"Nam phrik phao","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Nam phrik phao is a type of Thai chili sauce known as nam phrik. It contains chili peppers, shallots, garlic, fermented shrimp, tamarind, fish sauce and palm sugar."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-nam-phrik-phao"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nam_phrik_phao"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisi